From: Max <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: fix IPQ9574 Gen3 link training for non-compliant endpoints

The Qualcomm PCIe 2.9.0 architecture used on IPQ9574 requires
GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL for endpoints such as QCN9074.

In Linux 6.18, qcom_pcie_common_set_equalization() clears
GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL, causing receiver detection to fail
with LTSSM remaining in DETECT_QUIET.

Set GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL in qcom_pcie_common_set_equalization()
and allow endpoint power and receiver termination to settle after PERST deassertion.

Signed-off-by: Max <max@maxnet.lan>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom-common.c | 2 +-
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c        | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom-common.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom-common.c
@@ -31,7 +31,7 @@ void qcom_pcie_common_set_equalization(s
 		}
 
 		reg = dw_pcie_readl_dbi(pci, GEN3_RELATED_OFF);
-		reg &= ~GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL;
+		reg |= GEN3_RELATED_OFF_GEN3_ZRXDC_NONCOMPL;
 		reg &= ~GEN3_RELATED_OFF_RATE_SHADOW_SEL_MASK;
 		reg |= FIELD_PREP(GEN3_RELATED_OFF_RATE_SHADOW_SEL_MASK,
 			  speed - PCIE_SPEED_8_0GT);
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -305,6 +305,8 @@ static void qcom_ep_reset_deassert(struc
 	/* Ensure that PERST has been asserted for at least 100 ms */
 	msleep(PCIE_T_PVPERL_MS);
 	qcom_perst_assert(pcie, false);
+	/* Allow endpoint clock, power and receiver detect to settle */
+	msleep(PCIE_T_PVPERL_MS);
 }
 
 static int qcom_pcie_start_link(struct dw_pcie *pci)
